# REQUIRES: verilator
# The direct-HBM bridge (shell/rtl/foldsim_hbm_bridge.sv: asynchronous FIFOs
# on the five AXI channels, 512 bits in the kernel's clock to 256 bits in the
# port's) against Inputs/tb_hbm_bridge.sv: random bursts, strobes and ids,
# writes applied in AW order (W may lead its AW), reads checked against the
# master's image at their B's; clock ratios 2:1, 1:2, 2511:1777, 1:3, 3:1,
# handshakes stalled at random.
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique -DSIMULATION --top-module tb -Mdir %t/br %S/Inputs/tb_hbm_bridge.sv %S/../../shell/rtl/foldsim_hbm_bridge.sv > %t/br.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/br/Vtb +verilator+seed+1 +sp=2500 +mp=1250 +ops=1500 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/br/Vtb +verilator+seed+2 +sp=2500 +mp=1250 +stall=50 +hi=60 +ops=1500 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/br/Vtb +verilator+seed+3 +sp=1250 +mp=2500 +stall=30 +ops=1500 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/br/Vtb +verilator+seed+4 +sp=2511 +mp=1777 +stall=10 +ops=1500 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/br/Vtb +verilator+seed+5 +sp=997 +mp=3001 +stall=40 +hi=5 +ops=1500 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/br/Vtb +verilator+seed+6 +sp=3001 +mp=997 +hi=1 +ops=1500 | FileCheck %s
# CHECK-NOT: FAIL
# CHECK: {{[0-9]+}} writes, {{[0-9]+}} reads, {{[0-9]+}} read beats checked
# CHECK: PASS
